A) Create a scratch jest test at /dayjs/test/zz-cpf-verify.test.js (delete it when done) that imports dayjs from '../src', customParseFormat from '../src/plugin/customParseFormat', moment from 'moment', and the locales '../src/locale/zh-cn' and '../src/locale/en'; extends customParseFormat; then asserts (printing each pair with console.log):
   - describe('meridiem locale') / it('AM'): input '2018-05-02 上午 12:00' with format 'YYYY-MM-DD A hh:mm' and locale 'zh-cn': `dayjs(input, format, 'zh-cn').valueOf()` === `moment(input, format, 'zh-cn').valueOf()` and the formatted value is '2018-05-02T00:00:00+00:00';
   - it('PM'): input '2018-05-02 下午 12:00' same format/locale: equals moment and formats to '2018-05-02T12:00:00+00:00';
   - also '2018-05-02 下午 1:00' -> 13:00 and '2018-05-02 上午 1:00' -> 01:00, both equal to moment;
   - English still works: '2018-05-02 01:02:03.004 AM +01:00' with 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss.SSS A ZZ' equals moment; '2018-05-02 12:00 am' -> 00:00 and '2018-05-02 12:00 pm' -> 12:00 (format 'YYYY-MM-DD hh:mm a'), both equal to moment.
   Run `cd /dayjs && npx jest test/zz-cpf-verify.test.js --coverage=false --verbose` and report the output.
B) Run `cd /dayjs && npx jest test/plugin/customParseFormat.test.js --coverage=false --verbose` (baseline: 38 tests passing) and report.
C) Run `cd /dayjs && npx jest --testPathIgnorePatterns '/zz-' --coverage=false` and report the summary (baseline: 56 suites / 524 tests all passing). If you see failures in test/plugin/timezone.test.js or test/plugin/weekYear.test.js, report them separately as caused by concurrent agents and do NOT try to fix them.
